    {
      "id": "c2350503988d43c0b949c5b51625bde2",
      "type": "COMMENT",
      "position": {
        "x": -504.4962636332073,
        "y": -441.1113672607096
      },
      "data": {
        "text": "What?\n\nThis flow builds, signs, and sends a real Solana transaction that moves SOL from one address to another. You set the sender, the recipient, the amount, and the network. Pressing Send broadcasts it to the cluster and shows you the resulting transaction signature. "
      },
      "measured": {
        "width": 280,
        "height": 136
      },
      "selected": false,
      "dragging": false
    },
    {
      "id": "733f51c5a36544e88885730ccce813c4",
      "type": "COMMENT",
      "position": {
        "x": -161.15761267319186,
        "y": -471.1581216213947
      },
      "data": {
        "text": "Why?\n\nWhy every dapp boils down to this                                      Every \"write\" on Solana like buying an NFT, swapping tokens, opening a position, voting in a DAO, is just a signed transaction at the end of the day. Three pieces are always in play:                                                    \n- instructions (what should happen)                                                        \n- signers (who authorized it)                                                              \n- a recent blockhash (so the network knows it's fresh)                                     \nOnce you can compose those three, you can talk to ANY program on Solana."
      },
      "measured": {
        "width": 280,
        "height": 191
      },
      "selected": false,
      "dragging": false
    },
    {
      "id": "d80f8f3096e94dc8b4fa2e3da4c0dc85",
      "type": "COMMENT",
      "position": {
        "x": 197.16765014345677,
        "y": -424.9307559977404
      },
      "data": {
        "text": "You just sent your first programmatic Solana transaction. The signature the node returns is a permanent receipt. Paste it into any explorer                        and the world can verify your transfer happened. From here, swapping the System program for any other program (a token, a DEX, your own                           \n  custom contract) is a one-node change."
      },
      "measured": {
        "width": 280,
        "height": 122
      },
      "selected": false,
      "dragging": false
    }
